  "initial_failures": [
    "Initial App fixture incorrectly expected terminal failed; real started host errors become deferred uncertain / reconcile_pending. A journal fault trigger was also installed before lazy creation of its real table. Tests were corrected to the existing contract and trigger setup moved to the actual Watch attempt; production validation not weakened.",
    "Revised cold test incorrectly assumed fresh init/reload EnqueueRun admission would reject. The corrected test claims the fresh run and executes the real SDK: owner.open refuses old Active/Blocked before Watch, new run remains reconciliation-pending, old run remains unclaimable, files/history/notices unchanged."
  ],
  "runtime_evidence": [
    "Native Linux fault uses owned directories and closes the second spec descriptor so a real add-watch syscall fails. It proves attempted ordinal, no third-spec attempt and no inotify fd leak, not real resource exhaustion.",
    "Actual SDK init/reload and hardlink/STRM failure, ordinary error rejection, original fixed title/prefix, one local notice and independent receipt, no Router/queue/outbox/external send.",
    "SQL triggers test notice/journal/core-receipt rollback; private commit seam tests precommit failure, real committed SQL with lost ACK, and committed-corrupt receipt. Watch/commit counts and stored evidence are checked; the failed SDK state alone does not prove which diagnostic error returned.",
    "True App Close/New and restore owner/new SDK retry verify blocked recovery without reopening watches or repeating notices/deleting media. Two clone receipts reject cross-instance/generation/revision substitution."
  ],
